<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>kitchen_base_run_east</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>East wall run with a DOUBLE stainless sink (two 0.358 m bowls, 0.190 deep, sharing a divider) and a chrome faucet, positioned to sit under the east window, plus a 0.600 m appliance gap for the dishwasher on the far side of the sink. The counter runs over that gap and the toe kick under it. Counter 0.900 high x 0.635 deep, 0.600 carcass, and a 0.089 high x 0.076 deep toe kick (3.5" x 3", US standard) - deliberately lower than the 0.097 m robot, so it cannot drive in. Origin is the back (wall) face, centred on length, on the floor; the unit grows towards -y. Finishes match across the whole kitchen family: wood.png doors (from Cabinet), marble.png counters (from TableMarble), brushed stainless handles.</description>
</model>
